#
# The XGS 3300's fail-to-wire relay pair, Port1 and Port2, put back to normal at every boot where it
# is found in bypass, its watchdog expired or a trigger latched - scripts/xgs/ftw-normal.sh boot, with
# the vendor's open tool's own -t disable and -d, never arming anything. Early among the start hooks:
# while the pair bypasses, Port2 - the WAN this family is set up with - is joined to Port1 and not to
# this host, and the host's link on it stays up (measured 2026-11-11). Detached, because the
# coprocessor may still be coming up: it is asked every 15 s, twenty times at most, and the boot never
# waits. The script says what it found and did in the system log (tag xgs-ftw) and is quiet when
# there is nothing to do; it does nothing on any other board, and nothing at all where the kernel
# environment holds xgs.ftw.boot=0.
S=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/ftw-normal.sh
[ -f "${S}" ] || exit 0
/usr/sbin/daemon -f /bin/sh "${S}" boot
exit 0
